    "name": "Does a Kitchen Expansion in San Diego Require Permits?",
    "text": "Does a Kitchen Expansion in San Diego Require Permits?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Whether a kitchen expansion needs permits depends on the work involved and the local authority, but enlarging or altering a structure and changing regulated electrical, gas, mechanical, or plumbing systems generally requires permit review before construction. A contractor or design-build team should confirm the requirements for the property’s jurisdiction and include the needed plans and inspections in the project scope.",
